# a-word-that-waits

The rows are hidden and the word about them is committed to the outbox, and the process dies 
before the relay sends it. The orchestrator hears nothing, runs out of patience and commands 
the part again — and the relay may send the first word at any moment after that, or before 
it. Nothing orders the two, and the saga must come out of it having decided once. 

